--- An int past 64 bits grows: its digits are exact in both modes. (The
--- interpreter had wrapped it round silently, `crow build`'s optimized
--- binary did too, and only `crow run`'s debug build stopped; then both
--- modes stopped, until ints grew.)
big = 9223372036854775000
step = 800
log[big + step - step]
fn grow[n]
    return n * 1000
log[grow[big / 1000]]
log[grow[big]]
log[grow[grow[big]] / 1000000 eq big]
